`check_constant_columns` checks arrays of any shape: the columns are the second axis and further axes are pooled within each column, so a dead channel in epochs x channels x time data is a constant column; a 1-D array is one column. It returned nothing for anything but 2-D arrays, and `Report.add_container` passes the container's data as it is, so a report on epoch data never checked it. A new `names` argument labels an array's columns, which the report fills from the container's second dimension (channel or feature names instead of positions).
